# Task 2 – Customer Retention & Churn Analysis

## Business question
Why are customers leaving, which segments are most likely to churn, and what actions can improve retention?

## Data
- Telco customer churn dataset (`WA_Fn-UseC_-Telco-Customer-Churn`), raw customer and subscription data.

## Tool
- **Microsoft Excel** – cleaning, calculations, charts and dashboard (`Churn_Analysis_Dashboard_2026.xlsx`)

## Method
1. Cleaned and organized the customer data.
2. Calculated churn rate overall and by segment (contract, internet service, tech support, payment method).
3. Compared segments to find retention drivers.
4. Built a four-chart dashboard with an executive insights panel.

## Key insights
- **Overall churn is 26.5%.**
- **Contract length:** month-to-month customers churn at 42.7%, versus 11.3% on one-year and 2.8% on two-year contracts.
- **Tech support:** customers without it churn at 41.6%; with it, 15.1%.
- **Internet service:** fiber optic customers churn at 41.9%, more than double DSL at 18.9%.
- **Payment method:** electronic check users churn at 45.3%, against about 15–19% for automatic payment methods.

## Recommendations
1. Move month-to-month customers onto longer contracts with an incentive.
2. Bundle free tech support with fiber optic plans.
3. Investigate fiber optic service quality and pricing.
4. Offer a small discount for switching from manual to automatic payments.

